WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.880
"What Is the Safest
Metabolism Booster?"

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.900
Given the 60% surge in the
adrenal hormone noradrenaline

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.689
within minutes of just drinking
two cups of plain water,

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:22.340
might one get the weight loss
benefits of noradrenaline-releasing drugs

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.779
like ephedra, without the risks?

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:28.789
You don’t know until
you put it to the test.

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:30.519
Published in the Journal
of the Endocrine Society,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.560
the results were described
as “uniquely spectacular.”

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.220
Drinking two cups of water
increased the metabolic rate

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.570
of men and women by 30%.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.480
The increase started within 10 minutes

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.390
and reached a maximum within an hour.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.550
In the 90 minutes after drinking
a single tall glass of water,

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:51.050
the study subjects burned
about an extra 25 calories.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.060
Do that four times a day throughout
the day and you could wipe out

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.760
100 extra calories—more than ephedra!

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.150
You’d trim off more calories
drinking water than taking

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.760
weight loss doses of the
banned substance, ephedrine—

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.810
the active component of
ephedra—three times a day.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:13.040
And we’re just talking about plain,
cheap, safe, and legal tap water!

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.960
Using the 10 Calorie Rule I explained
previously, unless we somehow

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:21.100
compensated by eating more or
moving less, drinking that much water

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.810
could make us lose
10 pounds over time.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.850
“In essence,” concluded
one research team,

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:29.940
“water drinking provides
negative calories.”

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.660
A similar effect was found in
overweight and obese children.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.391
Drinking about two cups of
water led to a 25% increase

00:01:35.391 --> 00:01:38.950
in metabolic rate within
24 minutes, lasting at least

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.610
66 minutes until
the experiment ended.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:45.810
So, just getting the recommended
daily “adequate intake” of water—

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.780
about 7 cups a day for
children ages 4 through 8,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.010
and for ages 9 through 13,
8 cups a day for girls

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:58.420
and 10 cups for boys—may offer
more than just hydration benefits.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:02.060
Not all research teams were able
to replicate these findings, though.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:07.540
Others only found about a 10
to 20% increase, a 5% increase,

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:10.810
or effectively none at all,
pouring cold water,

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.280
one might say, on
the whole concept.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.200
What we care about,
though, is weight loss.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.860
The proof is in the pudding.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.560
Let’s test the waters, shall we?

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.880
Some researchers suggest,
“The increase in metabolic rate

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.670
with water drinking could
be systematically applied

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.020
in the prevention of weight gain….”

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.360
Talk about a safe, simple,
side-effect-free solution—

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.640
in fact free, in every sense.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.220
Drug companies may spend
billions getting a new drug to market,

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:42.200
surely a little could be
spared to test something that,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.840
at the very least, couldn’t hurt.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.060
That’s the problem, though.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.080
Water Is a “cost-free intervention.”

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.780
There are observational
studies suggesting those who drink,

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.780
for example, four or more
cups of water a day appear

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.710
to lose more weight, independent
of confounding factors

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:02.560
such as less soda or more exercise,
but you don’t really know...

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.640
until you put it to the test.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.680
And finally, in 2013, “Effect
of ‘Water Induced Thermogenesis’

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.599
on Body Weight, Body Mass
Index and Body Composition

00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:14.240
of Overweight Subjects.”

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.530
Fifty overweight
“girls” (actually women,

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.800
ages 18 through 23) were
asked to drink two cups of water

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.260
three times a day half an
hour before meals over

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.060
and above their regular
water intake, without otherwise

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.680
changing their diets
or physical activity.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.640
And, they lost an average
of three pounds in eight weeks.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.600
What happened to those
in the control group?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.490
There was no control group, a fatal
flaw for any weight loss study

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.349
due to the “Hawthorne effect,”
where just knowing you’re

00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:44.840
being watched and weighed may
subtly affect people’s behavior.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:49.150
Of course, we’re just talking
about water; so, with no downsides

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.959
one might as well give it a
try, but I’d feel more confident

00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:54.050
if there were some randomized,
controlled trials

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.270
to really put it to the test.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.640
Thankfully, there are!

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.060
Oh, I hate it when the
title ruins the suspense.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.880
Overweight and obese men and
women randomized to two cups

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.250
of water before each meal lost
nearly five pounds more body fat

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.909
in 12 weeks than those
in the control group.

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:14.599
Both groups were put on the
same calorie-restricted diet,

00:04:14.599 --> 00:04:21.850
but the one with the added
water lost weight 44% faster.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.780
A similar randomized controlled
trial found that about

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.040
1 in 4 in the water group lost
more than 5% of their body weight

00:04:27.041 --> 00:04:29.940
compared to only 1 in
20 in the control group.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.150
The average weight loss difference
was only about three pounds,

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.310
but those who claimed
to have actually complied

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.400
with the three-times-a-day instructions
lost about eight more pounds

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.850
compared to those only did
the extra water once a day or less.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.960
This is comparable to commercial
weight loss programs

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:50.560
like Weight Watchers, and all they
did was drink some extra water.

